[ext_resource type="Texture2D" path="res://assets/bonelight/ui/spells/lancet-metal.png" id="3_icon"]

; Lancet (scripts/Lancet.cs), 2026-11-09: a thin steel needle that always flies at the most wounded enemy in reach - by the
; share of its health lost, the nearest when none is hurt - and strikes harder the more it has lost, up to double; an
; ordinary enemy under a tenth of its health dies to it outright. Metal + Poison: a poison build's finisher. Nobody's opener;
; everyone earns it with the Shrike feat (enemies that die poisoned in one run). TargetingMode 10 is Wounded - the one spell
; that chooses by health - and DamageShape 1 a projectile.
;
; BaseDamage is ONE NEEDLE on a fresh body (Lancet.WoundedDamage doubles it on one with nothing left). BaseCooldown is the
; throw (the ONE fire loop): a fast timer, Hunter's Draw's and Sleet Runes' band. BaseProjectileCount is the needles a cast
; throws (plus Amount), one body each. BaseRange is the reach it chooses in: the middle band (.ai/spell-roster.md section 1),
; Folio's and Chain Lightning's.
;
; FIRST GUESSES, untuned. Spells start small (Eric, 2026-11-02): one needle at level 1, two at 3, three at 6. Written out in
; full so Player.EnsureRelevantLevelUps generates nothing of its own (ScalingTagsMask 27: Damage, Cooldown, Range,
; ProjectileCount): every level adds damage, even levels shorten the throw by 0.05 s, and 5 adds reach. Level 8: 14 a needle
; on a fresh body, three needles every 0.65 s, over 340.

